  "interpretation": [
    "The aligned PRISM route has measurable correct-caption sensitivity. Native conditioning wins all 24 repeated controls in each split; PRISM wins 18 training and 16 heldout controls.",
    "Averaging each caption across its three timesteps, the gap is positive for 7 of 8 training captions and 5 of 8 heldout captions. The positive mean does not show consistent improvement on every caption.",
    "Matched-caption flow MSE remains 48.5% higher on training pairs and 49.3% higher on heldout pairs than native conditioning with the same original DiT. Feature alignment alone has not recovered native denoising behavior.",
    "The earlier raw-overfit256 diagnostic used an adapted DiT and raw prompts. Comparing its PRISM metrics to this chat/original-DiT run is not an isolated ablation of feature alignment.",
    "Image quality must be assessed separately from these losses. This quantitative analysis does not establish successful tiny-set image overfitting or justify treating the connector as quality-qualified."
  ]
